# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.17 slice 4 — G3: `g2_structural_guard.ebnf` plus a TRAILING guard.
#
# ⛔ ONE-DIFFERENCE CONTROL against G2. Byte-for-byte `g2_structural_guard.ebnf` except that the
# same lookahead is ALSO applied once after the whole rewritten body:
#
#   G2:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix &( tick lparen lit rparen ) )*
#   G3:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix &( tick lparen lit rparen ) )* &( tick lparen lit rparen )
#                                                                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. G2 closes every starvation the `*` causes and still REJECTS `e5`
# (`k = t'(n);`) — because that one is not caused by the `*` at all. Bisected in slice 4: `e5`
# rejects even with the quantifier deleted outright. The over-long match comes from `prim_base`'s
# own sheared-clone alternative (`cast_seed`, i.e. `constant_cast` over a shorn `casting_type`)
# winning the `ct` tournament outright, after which the holder has no residual left and the choice
# never gives back ([[project_pgen_gives_back_at_the_choice_but_not_at_the_quantifier]], as
# CORRECTED by this slice).
#
# ⭐⭐ WHAT THE TRAILING GUARD DOES ABOUT IT. It moves the follow restriction from "each iteration"
# to "the rule's whole result", so an over-long match from the SEED is refused exactly as an
# over-long match from the LOOP is. Refusing it makes the `prim` branch FAIL rather than win, and a
# failed branch is not a losing branch — the tournament then has only `kw` left and picks it. ⇒ the
# repair needs no give-back at the choice, which is the property that made (iii) affordable in the
# first place; it converts a would-be give-back into a branch failure the existing selection already
# handles.
#
# ⛔ IT IS STILL A CALL-SITE CONSTRUCT, and `g4_trailing_guard_needs_a_clone.ebnf` measures that:
# written onto the RULE it breaks every holder that wants the whole run — Q5's law, at the new
# position. This file has exactly one holder, so the clone is degenerate here and the distinction is
# invisible; G4/G5 supply it.
@entry: true
scratch := kw_k eq outer_cast semi
outer_cast := ct tick lparen lit rparen
ct := kw | prim
prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix &( tick lparen lit rparen ) )* &( tick lparen lit rparen )
prim_base := lit | cast_seed
cast_seed := kw tick lparen lit rparen
prim_suffix := tick lparen lit rparen

lit := trivia /n/
kw := trivia /t/
kw_k := trivia /k/
eq := trivia "="
semi := trivia ";"
tick := trivia "'"
lparen := trivia "("
rparen := trivia ")"

@branch_policy: priority_first
trivia := (line_comment | block_comment)*
line_comment := /\/\/[^\n]*(\n|$)/
block_comment := /\/\*([^*]|\*+[^*\/])*\*+\//
